From 27802a823bde85571f594fc5620127d7d893f822 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:13:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Validate host-derived network config before checkpointing

Add an optional cloudprovider.NetworkConfigValidator interface. When the
cloud provider implements it, DraNet passes the final network
configuration of a netdev device, including the routes, rules and
neighbors derived from the host, to the provider right before persisting
it with SetDeviceConfig. If the provider rejects it, the device
preparation fails through PrepareResult.Err, the interface stays in the
host namespace, any allocated profile is released and kubelet retries.

Providers that do not implement the interface keep the current behavior.
The hook is read-only and does not add any provider-specific routing
logic.

Fixes #278
